   "path": "SCENE.md",
   "role": "instructions",
   "content": "# Slide Swap\n\nScenes swap on one canvas, never overlapping: the old scene is shoved off under power and the next one springs in and brakes into place. Plays three scenes (A, B, C). Built-in placeholder scenes A, B and C (the three .ssw-panel elements) make it preview on its own; to use it with your own scenes, replace the contents of those panels (each holds for 70 frames) and keep the block on a track above.\n\nCategory: transitions. Length: 7.0 s. WebGL: no.\n\nUse when:\n- Slide-deck style content with several scenes that should swap crisply.\n- UI walkthroughs where scenes slide in like screens.\n\nAvoid when:\n- You need the scenes to overlap or crossfade.\n- Cinematic pieces that want depth rather than flat slides.\n\nVariables:\n- axis (enum): Axis, default \"x\"\n- in_distance (number, 0-1): In distance, default 0.28\n- out_distance (number, 0-1): Out distance, default 0.1\n- slide_frames (number, 6-60): Slide frames, default 30\n\nSource: https://github.com/Remocn/remocn. Licence: MIT. The scene file keeps the upstream notice.\n"
  },
  {
   "path": "scene.html",
   "role": "source",
   "content": "<!doctype html>\n<!--\n  Slide Swap\n\n  Scenes swap on one canvas, never overlapping: the old scene is shoved off under power and the next one springs in and brakes into place. Plays three scenes (A, B, C).\n\n  Ported to an HTML + GSAP sub-composition by usemosio/blocks from:\n  https://github.com/Remocn/remocn/blob/126221ae00ba86eb40b65731b125ff398687d3b7/registry/remocn/slide-swap/index.tsx\n\n  MIT License\n\n  Copyright (c) 2026 Remocn\n\n  Permission is hereby granted, free of charge, to any person obtaining a copy\n  of this software and associated documentation files (the \"Software\"), to deal\n  in the Software without restriction, including without limitation the rights\n  to use, copy, modify, merge, publish, distribute, sublicense, and/or sell\n  copies of the Software, and to permit persons to whom the Software is\n  furnished to do so, subject to the following conditions:\n\n  The above copyright notice and this permission notice shall be included in all\n  copies or substantial portions of the Software.\n\n  THE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED \"AS IS\", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR\n  IMPLIED, INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO THE WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY,\n  FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE AND NONINFRINGEMENT. IN NO EVENT SHALL THE\n  AUTHORS OR COPYRIGHT HOLDERS BE LIABLE FOR ANY CLAIM, DAMAGES OR OTHER\n  LIABILITY, WHETHER IN AN ACTION OF CONTRACT, TORT OR OTHERWISE, ARISING FROM,\n  OUT OF OR IN CONNECTION WITH THE SOFTWARE OR THE USE OR OTHER DEALINGS IN THE\n  SOFTWARE.\n-->\n<html\n  lang=\"en\"\n  data-composition-id=\"slide-swap\"\n  data-composition-duration=\"7.0\"\n  data-composition-variables='[\n  {\n    \"id\": \"axis\",\n    \"type\": \"enum\",\n    \"role\": \"motion\",\n    \"label\": \"Axis\",\n    \"description\": \"Direction scenes travel along.\",\n    \"default\": \"x\",\n    \"options\": [\n      {\n        \"value\": \"x\",\n        \"label\": \"Horizontal\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"value\": \"y\",\n        \"label\": \"Vertical\"\n      }\n    ]\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"in_distance\",\n    \"type\": \"number\",\n    \"role\": \"motion\",\n    \"label\": \"In distance\",\n    \"description\": \"How far the incoming scene starts away, as a fraction of the frame size.\",\n    \"default\": 0.28,\n    \"min\": 0,\n    \"max\": 1,\n    \"step\": 0.01\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"out_distance\",\n    \"type\": \"number\",\n    \"role\": \"motion\",\n    \"label\": \"Out distance\",\n    \"description\": \"How far the outgoing scene is shoved, as a fraction of the frame size.\",\n    \"default\": 0.1,\n    \"min\": 0,\n    \"max\": 1,\n    \"step\": 0.01\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"slide_frames\",\n    \"type\": \"number\",\n    \"role\": \"motion\",\n    \"label\": \"Slide frames\",\n    \"description\": \"Frames (at 30 fps) the entrance slide lasts.\",\n    \"default\": 30,\n    \"min\": 6,\n    \"max\": 60,\n    \"step\": 1\n  }\n]'\n>\n  <head>\n    <meta charset=\"UTF-8\" />\n    <title>Slide Swap</title>\n  </head>\n  <body>\n    <template>\n      <link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Geist:wght@400;500;600;700&amp;display=block\" />\n      <style>\n        #root {\n          position: absolute;\n          inset: 0;\n          overflow: hidden;\n          container-type: size;\n          font-family: var(--font-display, Geist, system-ui, sans-serif);\n          pointer-events: none;\n        }\n\n        #root { background: #141318; }\n        .ssw-stage { position: absolute; inset: 0; }\n        .ssw-panel { position: absolute; inset: 0; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; overflow: hidden; }\n        .ssw-in { display: flex; flex-direction: column; align-items: center; gap: 2.4cqmin; }\n        .ssw-in span { font-size: 9cqmin; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: -0.03em; line-height: 1; color: #f2f2f2; white-space: nowrap; }\n        .ssw-bar { display: block; width: 14cqmin; height: 0.8cqmin; border-radius: 1cqmin; background: rgba(242, 242, 242, 0.55); }\n        .ssw-pa { background: #141318; }\n        .ssw-pb { background: linear-gradient(135deg, #3b3699 0%, #1e2a6b 55%, #0f4c75 100%); }\n        .ssw-pc { background: linear-gradient(135deg, #7a2f5f 0%, #3a2250 55%, #1c1b3f 100%); }\n\n        .ssw-panel { display: none; }\n\n      </style>\n\n      <div id=\"root\" data-composition-id=\"slide-swap\" data-duration=\"7.0\" data-fps=\"30\">\n        <div id=\"ssw-clip\" class=\"ssw-stage clip\" data-start=\"0\" data-duration=\"7.0\" data-track-index=\"0\">\n          <div id=\"ssw-a\" class=\"ssw-panel ssw-pa\"><div class=\"ssw-in\"><span>Scene A</span><i class=\"ssw-bar\"></i></div></div>\n          <div id=\"ssw-b\" class=\"ssw-panel ssw-pb\"><div class=\"ssw-in\"><span>Scene B</span><i class=\"ssw-bar\"></i></div></div>\n          <div id=\"ssw-c\" class=\"ssw-panel ssw-pc\"><div class=\"ssw-in\"><span>Scene C</span><i class=\"ssw-bar\"></i></div></div>\n        </div>\n\n        <script src=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/gsap@3.14.2/dist/gsap.min.js\"></script>\n        \n        <script>\n          (function () {\n            \"use strict\";\n\nvar root = document.getElementById(\"root\");\nvar vars = window.__hyperframes && window.__hyperframes.getVariables ? window.__hyperframes.getVariables() : {};\nfunction num(v, f, min, max) { var n = Number(v); return Number.isFinite(n) ? Math.min(max, Math.max(min, n)) : f; }\nfunction str(v, f) { return typeof v === \"string\" && v.trim() ? v.trim() : f; }\nfunction pick(v, list, f) { return list.indexOf(String(v)) >= 0 ? String(v) : f; }\nfunction clamp01(x) { return x < 0 ? 0 : x > 1 ? 1 : x; }\nfunction lerp(a, b, t) { return a + (b - a) * t; }\nfunction smooth(a, b, x) { var t = clamp01((x - a) / (b - a)); return t * t * (3 - 2 * t); }\n// cubic-bezier easing, solved by bisection (pure function of x)\nfunction bez(x1, y1, x2, y2) {\n  return function (x) {\n    if (x <= 0) return 0;\n    if (x >= 1) return 1;\n    var lo = 0, hi = 1, t = x;\n    for (var i = 0; i < 28; i++) {\n      var cx = 3 * (1 - t) * (1 - t) * t * x1 + 3 * (1 - t) * t * t * x2 + t * t * t;\n      if (cx < x) lo = t; else hi = t;\n      t = (lo + hi) / 2;\n    }\n    return 3 * (1 - t) * (1 - t) * t * y1 + 3 * (1 - t) * t * t * y2 + t * t * t;\n  };\n}\nvar inOutEase = bez(0.42, 0, 0.58, 1);\nfunction inCubic(x) { return x * x * x; }\nfunction outCubic(x) { return 1 - Math.pow(1 - x, 3); }\nfunction inQuad(x) { return x * x; }\nfunction outQuad(x) { return 1 - (1 - x) * (1 - x); }\nfunction outBack(s) { return function (x) { return 1 + (s + 1) * Math.pow(x - 1, 3) + s * Math.pow(x - 1, 2); }; }\n// interpolate(p, inputs, outputs, ease): clamped, eased per segment (like a frame interpolate)\nfunction interp(p, xs, ys, ease) {\n  var n = xs.length;\n  if (p <= xs[0]) return ys[0];\n  if (p >= xs[n - 1]) return ys[n - 1];\n  for (var i = 1; i < n; i++) {\n    if (p <= xs[i]) {\n      var t = (p - xs[i - 1]) / (xs[i] - xs[i - 1]);\n      if (ease) t = ease(t);\n      return lerp(ys[i - 1], ys[i], t);\n    }\n  }\n  return ys[n - 1];\n}\nfunction mulberry32(a) {\n  return function () {\n    a |= 0; a = (a + 0x6d2b79f5) | 0;\n    var t = Math.imul(a ^ (a >>> 15), 1 | a);\n    t = (t + Math.imul(t ^ (t >>> 7), 61 | t)) ^ t;\n    return ((t ^ (t >>> 14)) >>> 0) / 4294967296;\n  };\n}\n// damped spring from 0 to 1 (zero initial velocity), t in seconds\nfunction spring(t, damping, stiffness, mass) {\n  if (t <= 0) return 0;\n  var w0 = Math.sqrt(stiffness / mass), z = damping / (2 * Math.sqrt(stiffness * mass));\n  if (Math.abs(z - 1) < 1e-4) return 1 - Math.exp(-w0 * t) * (1 + w0 * t);\n  if (z < 1) {\n    var wd = w0 * Math.sqrt(1 - z * z);\n    return 1 - Math.exp(-z * w0 * t) * (Math.cos(wd * t) + (z * w0 / wd) * Math.sin(wd * t));\n  }\n  var s = Math.sqrt(z * z - 1), r1 = -w0 * (z - s), r2 = -w0 * (z + s);\n  return 1 - (r2 * Math.exp(r1 * t) - r1 * Math.exp(r2 * t)) / (r2 - r1);\n}\nfunction stripIds(node) {\n  var all = node.querySelectorAll(\"[id]\");\n  for (var i = 0; i < all.length; i++) all[i].removeAttribute(\"id\");\n  node.removeAttribute(\"id\");\n  return node;\n}\nfunction drive(name, duration, frame) {\n  var st = { p: 0 };\n  frame(0);\n  var tl = gsap.timeline({ paused: true });\n  tl.to(st, { p: 1, duration: duration, ease: \"none\", onUpdate: function () { frame(st.p); } }, 0);\n  tl.seek(0);\n  window.__timelines = window.__timelines || {};\n  window.__timelines[name] = tl;\n}\n\n            var D = 7.0;\n\nvar axis = pick(vars.axis, [\"x\", \"y\"], \"x\"), inDist = num(vars.in_distance, 0.28, 0, 1), outDist = num(vars.out_distance, 0.1, 0, 1);\nvar slideFrames = Math.round(num(vars.slide_frames, 30, 6, 60));\nvar SCENE = 70, OUT = 22, FADE_IN = 24, N = 3, TOTAL = SCENE * N;\nvar panels = [document.getElementById(\"ssw-a\"), document.getElementById(\"ssw-b\"), document.getElementById(\"ssw-c\")];\nvar size = axis === \"x\" ? root.clientWidth : root.clientHeight;\nfunction tr(v) { return axis === \"x\" ? v + \"px 0\" : \"0 \" + v + \"px\"; }\nfunction frame(p) {\n  var f = Math.min(Math.floor(p * TOTAL), TOTAL - 1), idx = Math.min(N - 1, Math.floor(f / SCENE)), local = f - idx * SCENE;\n  var exits = idx < N - 1, enters = idx > 0, trans = \"0 0\", op = 1;\n  if (exits && local >= SCENE - OUT) {\n    var t = Math.min((local - (SCENE - OUT)) / OUT, 1);\n    trans = tr(-outDist * size * Math.pow(t, 5)); op = 1 - t * t;\n  } else if (enters && local + 1 < slideFrames) {\n    var e = local + 1, sp = Math.min(1, spring(e / 30, 60, 300, 0.5)), tf = Math.min(Math.max(e / FADE_IN, 0), 1);\n    trans = tr(inDist * size * (1 - sp)); op = 1 - (1 - tf) * (1 - tf);\n  }\n  for (var i = 0; i < N; i++) {\n    panels[i].style.display = i === idx ? \"flex\" : \"none\";\n    if (i === idx) { panels[i].style.translate = trans; panels[i].style.opacity = op; }\n  }\n}\n\n            drive(\"slide-swap\", D, frame);\n          })();\n        </script>\n      </div>\n    </template>\n  </body>\n</html>\n"
  }
 ],
